  "description": "General identical-nucleon symmetrization infra for ANY isotope (Z,N) via the Frobenius power-sum formula h_Z=Σ_μ p_μ/z_μ (bosonic), e_Z=Σ_μ ε_μ p_μ/z_μ (fermionic/Pauli), with p_k=tr_M(B_p^k) (proton core braid^k, an H₃ Markov trace carrying the y_λ Wedderburn weights). Generalizes the Z=2 scalar probe (h₂/e₂) to all Z,N: compute p_1..p_{max Z,N} ONCE per nucleon (H₃ cost), then the Frobenius sum is pure partition arithmetic. Replaces the naive distinguishable τ_p^Z·τ_n^N constituent (closed_form_tau_M.py:302, identity term μ=(1^Z) only) with the correctly (anti)symmetrized h_Z(p)h_N(n) / e_Z(p)e_N(n). SCALAR CAVEAT: this approximates (≠) the exact block-level q-Young projection into H_{3Z} (small-Z refinement); it is the tractable GENERAL infra. Schur-Weyl Z=2,3,4 verified in QOU.Hecke.IdenticalParticleSymmetrization.",
